{"path":"filesystem/hard_link_count","title":"std::filesystem::hard_link_count","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::filesystem::</span>hard_link_count","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/filesystem/hard_link_count","section":"filesystem","kind":"page","summary":"Returns the number of hard links for the filesystem object identified by path p.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/filesystem\">&lt;filesystem&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw139\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uintmax_t</span></span></a> hard_link_count<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/path\"><span class=\"kw2219\">std::<span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw139\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uintmax_t</span></span></a> hard_link_count<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/path\"><span class=\"kw2219\">std::<span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\"><span class=\"kw881\">std::<span class=\"me2\">error_code</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns the number of hard links for the filesystem object identified by path <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code>.\n</p><p>The non-throwing overload returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">static_cast</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>uintmax_t<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> on errors.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> path to examine\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ec\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> out-parameter for error reporting in the non-throwing overload\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The number of hard links for <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>Any overload not marked <code>noexcept</code> may throw <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\">std::bad_alloc</a></span> if memory allocation fails.<br>\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Throws <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/filesystem_error\">std::filesystem::filesystem_error</a></span> on underlying OS API errors, constructed with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> as the first path argument and the OS error code as the error code argument.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Sets a <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\"><span class=\"kw881\">std::<span class=\"me2\">error_code</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> parameter to the OS API error code if an OS API call fails, and executes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ec.</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code/clear\"><code>clear</code></a><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> if no errors occur.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;filesystem&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> fs <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// On a POSIX-style filesystem, each directory has at least 2 hard links:</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// itself and the special member pathname \".\"</span>\n    fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">current_path</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Number of hard links for current path is \"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">hard_link_count</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// Each \"..\" is a hard link to the parent directory, so the total number</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// of hard links for any directory is 2 plus number of direct subdirectories</span>\n    p <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">current_path</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"..\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// Each dot-dot is a hard link to parent</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Number of hard links for .. is \"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">hard_link_count</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Number of hard links for current path is 2\nNumber of hard links for .. is 3</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/create_hard_link\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>create_hard_link</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  creates a hard link <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/directory_entry/hard_link_count\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>hard_link_count</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the number of hard links referring to the file to which the directory entry refers <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::filesystem::directory_entry</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"filesystem","title":"Filesystem library (since C++17)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::filesystem::hard_link_count","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++17. Returns the number of hard links for the filesystem object identified by path p."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"p, ec"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The number of hard links for p."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Any overload not marked noexcept may throw std::bad_alloc if memory allocation fails."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"create_hard_link","note":"creates a hard link"},{"label":"hard_link_count","note":"returns the number of hard links referring to the file to which the directory entry refers"}]}]},"standards":["C++17"],"wordCount":293,"codeBlockCount":2}
